  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for people who can check numbers and explain them simply. They judge you by accuracy, clear assumptions and how well you spot errors.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing the formula next to every number you report.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and everyday maths for business careers: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools calculate and draft summaries instantly. Routine calculation shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Checking results, spotting wrong assumptions and explaining numbers hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to calculate and check; later, own the reasoning.
  </p>

